s of the Devonian.&nbsp; NCU incorporated HNH (in part; 2002); NCATG (in full, 2025); and SAPCL (in full, 2025).","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/ncu.jpg","url":"https://ncbg.unc.edu/research/unc-herbarium/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=206","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/ncu-vascularplants_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"mccormick@unc.edu"},{"first_name":"Carol Ann","last_name":"McCormick","role":"Herbarium Curatrix","email":"mccormick@unc.edu"},{"first_name":"Alan","last_name":"Weakley","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"weakley@unc.edu"},{"first_name":"Shanna","last_name":"Oberreiter","role":"Herbarium Assistant Curatrix","email":"oberreit@email.unc.edu"},{"first_name":"Carol Ann","last_name":"McCormick","role":"Herbarium Curatrix","email":"mccormick@unc.edu"},{"first_name":"Alan","last_name":"Weakley","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"weakley@unc.edu"},{"first_name":"Shanna","last_name":"Oberreiter","role":"Herbarium Assistant Curatrix","email":"oberreit@email.unc.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":457697,"hitRatio":0.000006554554650784252},{"uuid":"7450a9e3-ef95-4f9e-8260-09b498d2c5e6","itemCount":3,"name":"Harvard University Herbaria: All Records","description":"This dataset contains all digitized specimen records stewarded by the Harvard University Herbaria. \n\nThe Harvard University Herbaria, with over 5 million specimens, is the world’s largest University Herbaria. Included in the Herbaria are what were once six separate herbarium collections: * Herbarium of the Arnold Arboretum (A) * Economic Herbarium of Oakes Ames (ECON) * Oakes Ames Orchid Herbarium (AMES) * Farlow Herbarium (FH) * Gray Herbarium (GH) * New England Botanical Club Herbarium (NEBC).\n\nDarwinCore data follows the AppleCore guidance https://code.google.com/p/applecore/.","url":"","emllink":"https://ipt.huh.harvard.edu/ipt/eml.do?r=huh_all_records","archivelink":"https://ipt.huh.harvard.edu/ipt/archive.do?r=huh_all_records","contacts":[{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Kennedy","role":"Director of Biodiversity Informatics","email":"jonathan_kennedy@harvard.edu"},{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Kennedy","role":"Director of Biodiversity Informatics","email":"jonathan_kennedy@harvard.edu"},{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Kennedy","role":"Director of Biodiversity Informatics","email":"jonathan_kennedy@harvard.edu"},{"first_name":"Michaela","last_name":"Schmull","role":"Director of Collections","email":"mschmull@oeb.harvard.edu"},{"first_name":"Charles","last_name":"Davis","role":"Curator of Vascular Plant Collection; Professor of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology","email":"cdavis@oeb.harvard.edu"},{"first_name":"Jeannine","last_name":"Cavender-Bares","role":"Director of the Harvard University Herbaria; Professor of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology"},{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Kennedy","role":"Director of Biodiversity Informatics","email":"jonathan_kennedy@harvard.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY","publisher":"a8dbdab2-4e17-47d4-b051-d37552bf2396","totalCount":2048583,"hitRatio":0.0000014644268745762314},{"uuid":"33bac15d-b1d0-42a1-8801-86149887eeef","itemCount":2,"name":"Berry College Herbarium","description":"","url":"https://www.berry.edu","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=440","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/bch_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"mcipollini@berry.edu"},{"last_name":"Martin Cipollini","email":"mcipollini@berry.edu"},{"last_name":"Martin Cipollini","email":"mcipollini@berry.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":2829,"hitRatio":0.0007069635913750442},{"uuid":"beab5209-9628-4d4d-851e-2bc9bb1a0105","itemCount":2,"name":"University of Georgia Herbarium","description":"","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/ga_new.jpg","url":"https://www.plantbio.uga.edu/uga-herbarium","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=258","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/ga_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"tanisha.williams1@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Tanisha","last_name":"Williams","role":"Curator/Director","email":"tanisha.williams1@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Steven","last_name":"Hughes","role":"Collections Manager","email":"sthughes@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Tanisha","last_name":"Williams","role":"Curator/Director","email":"tanisha.williams1@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Steven","last_name":"Hughes","role":"Collections Manager","email":"sthughes@uga.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":280846,"hitRatio":0.000007121340521139699},{"uuid":"120d557c-c5be-474d-98f0-1ba00ae16b40","itemCount":1,"name":"University of Tennessee, Chattanooga Herbarium","description":"Vascular Herbarium at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/ucht.jpg","url":null,"emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=311","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/utc-ucht_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"joey-shaw@utc.edu"},{"first_name":"Joey","last_name":"Shaw","role":"Herbarium Curator","email":"joey-shaw@utc.edu"},{"first_name":"Joey","last_name":"Shaw","role":"Herbarium Curator","email":"joey-shaw@utc.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":49090,"hitRatio":0.000020370747606437155},{"uuid":"4523e216-ee13-4b15-a3f7-a6fd56431604","itemCount":1,"name":"Louisiana State University, Shirley C. Tucker Herbarium - Vascular Plants","description":"Shirley C. Tucker Herbarium at Louisiana State University, Vascular Plant Collection contains 310,000+ specimens. Several regional herbaria are integrated entirely or in part, including NO, LSUS, MCN, NLU, Eglin Air Force Base, and New Orleans Academy of Sciences. Only Tulane University Herbarium (NO) remains a distinct collection.&nbsp;&nbsp;Geographic distribution is global, but strengths are Louisiana and the southeastern USA, southen California, Colorado Rocky Mountains, Yucatan Peninsula, Colombia and Brazil. Families well-represented include Asteraceae, Fabaceae, Cyperaceae, Rubiaceae, and Poaceae. Significant collectors include: Fr. G. Ars&egrave;ne, L. M. Booth,&nbsp;C. A. Brown,&nbsp;I. W. Clokey, R. S. Cocks, D. Demaree,&nbsp;J. A. Ewan,&nbsp;A. Featherman,&nbsp;A. Gray, J. Hale, J. F. Joor, D. D. Keck, E. P. Killip, J. G. Lemmon, Y. E. J. Mexia, F. W. Peirson,&nbsp;N. F. Peterson,&nbsp;J. L. Riddell, and D. Stone,&nbsp;R. D. Thomas, S. C. Tucker, L. E. Urbatsch, I. V&eacute;lez, and E. C. Wurzlow.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/lsu.jpg","url":"http://www.herbarium.lsu.edu/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=210","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/lsu-vascularplants_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"jkluse@lsu.edu"},{"last_name":"Jennifer S. Kluse, Collections Manager","email":"jkluse@lsu.edu"},{"last_name":"Jennifer S. Kluse, Collections Manager","email":"jkluse@lsu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC3 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":316835,"hitRatio":0.0000031562169583537174},{"uuid":"781fd581-7b93-471e-a025-413e4bcd8491","itemCount":1,"name":"University of Florida Herbarium (FLAS)","description":"The University of Florida Herbarium (FLAS) in the Florida Museum of Natural History contains approximately 500,000 specimens of vascular plants, bryophytes, lichens, fungi, and wood, with the earliest specimens dating to the early to mid-1800s. The FLAS acronym is the standard international abbreviation for the Herbarium, derived from its early association with the Florida Agricultural Experiment Station. The herbarium was established in 1891 by Peter H. Rolfs of Florida Agricultural College in Lake City, and later moved to the University of Florida in Gainesville in 1906. The vascular plant collection (ca. 320,000 specimens) has an excellent representation of the USA (esp. Florida and the southeastern USA), the West Indies (esp. Hispaniola), and other Neotropical areas. The bryophyte collection (ca. 70,000 specimens) and lichen collection (ca. 16,000 specimens) are worldwide in scope (esp. Florida and Neotropical areas such as Costa Rica, Venezuela, and Brazil). The wood collection (ca. 16,000 specimens) is worldwide in scope (esp. tropical woods). The algal collection includes ca. 3,500 specimens, mainly from Florida. The Fungal Herbarium contains ca. 55,000 specimens (primarily non-lichenized fungi and slime molds). This digital dataset serves the vascular plant collection, of which ca. 2/3 are digitized, including ca. 500 type specimens (holo-, lecto-, iso-, neo-, or epi-types). The herbarium's digitization effort has been supported by several institutions, including the Florida Museum of Natural History, Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences, National Science Foundation, United States Department of Agriculture (Hatch Project FLAS-HRB-04170), UF Libraries Digital Library Center, Florida Center for Library Automation, Florida Museum Associates, and the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation.","url":"","emllink":"https://ipt.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/ipt/eml.do?r=herbarium","archivelink":"https://ipt.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/ipt/archive.do?r=herbarium","contacts":[{"first_name":"Alan R.","last_name":"Franck","role":"Herbarium Collection Manager","email":"francka@flmnh.ufl.edu"},{"first_name":"Alan R.","last_name":"Franck","role":"Herbarium Collection Manager","email":"francka@flmnh.ufl.edu"},{"first_name":"Alan R.","last_name":"Franck","role":"Herbarium Collection Manager","email":"francka@flmnh.ufl.edu"},{"first_name":"Alan R.","last_name":"Franck","role":"Herbarium Collection Manager","email":"francka@flmnh.ufl.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"350857a8-4940-4d02-ad42-49557f8006f1","totalCount":287914,"hitRatio":0.0000034732593760636857},{"uuid":"92e4e092-6dcb-46bc-85a0-dea8310aba45","itemCount":1,"name":"Troy Herbarium Specimens from Morphbank","description":"Specimen Information and Images in the Morphbank repository from herarium specimens housed in the Troy State University (Alabama) Herbarium (TROY). 14,534 records in total. Digitized as part of the The Deep South Plant Specimen Imaging Project. http://www.nsf.gov/awardsearch/showAward?AWD_ID=0646222","url":"http://spectrum.troy.edu/herbarium/","emllink":"http://services.morphbank.net/ipt-2.0.4/eml.do?r=troyherbarium","archivelink":"http://services.morphbank.net/ipt-2.0.4/archive.do?r=troyherbarium","contacts":[{"first_name":"Greg","last_name":"Riccardi","role":"Director","email":"griccardi@fsu.edu"},{"first_name":"Deborah","last_name":"Paul","role":"Manager","email":"dpaul@fsu.edu"}],"data_rights":"Unknown License, assume Public Domain","publisher":"1a3c16b9-e699-439d-9ded-89dbbc84a100","totalCount":14534,"hitRatio":0.0000688041832943443},{"uuid":"e36691ec-c4f8-4bec-b331-b48ffa82ff49","itemCount":1,"name":"UTEP Plants (Arctos)","description":"The Herbarium contains well over 82,000 catalogued plant specimens. Overall geographic content of the Herbarium is approximately as follows: Texas, 24%; New Mexico, 22%; other USA, 32%; Mexico, 7%; other world, 15%. Herbarium materials at UTEP that are of special interest include an extensive representation of the floras of the desert mountain ranges of southern New Mexico and western Texas partially from a thorough floral survey and inventory across an east-west transect running from the Guadalupe/Davis Mountains of Texas to the Chiricahua Mountains of Arizona; voucher samples of specimens from which nectar samples were collected for the nectar chemistry research of C. E. Freeman and W. H. Reid; a seed collection, representing more than 800 species of mostly Southwestern taxa with individual samples mounted on slides and cross-indexed to their source sheets in the main herbarium collection; a cryptogamic collection in excess of 650 specimens, predominately lichens and mosses from various areas in southwestern North America, with significant collections of local specimens used for baseline data in studies by R. D. Worthington and his students on air pollution effects in the El Paso/Ciudad Juarez area; a synoptic collection from White Sands National Monument, representing survey work performed by W. H. Reid during the early 1970's.","url":"http://www.utep.edu/biodiversity/collections/herbarium.html https://ipt.vertnet.org/archive.do?r=utep_herb","emllink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/eml.do?r=utep_herb","archivelink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/archive.do?r=utep_herb","contacts":[{"first_name":"Teresa","last_name":"Mayfield-Meyer","role":"Collection Data Volunteer, UTEP Biodiversity Collections","email":"tmayfield.utepbc@jegelewicz.net"},{"first_name":"Vicky","last_name":"Zhuang","role":"Manager, UTEP Biodiversity Collections","email":"mzhuang@utep.edu"},{"first_name":"Teresa","last_name":"Mayfield-Meyer","role":"Collection Data Volunteer, UTEP Biodiversity Collections","email":"tmayfield.utepbc@jegelewicz.net"},{"first_name":"Vicky","last_name":"Zhuang","role":"Manager, UTEP Biodiversity Collections","email":"mzhuang@utep.edu"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Bloom","role":"Coordinator","email":"dbloom@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"Dusty","last_name":"McDonald","role":"Arctos Database Programmer","email":"dlmcdonald@alaska.edu"},{"first_name":"Vicky","last_name":"Zh